From: ACK72 <ACK72@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: fix channel completion and NPU recovery failure handling

diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/9999-y-mt76-recovery-lifecycle.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/9999-y-mt76-recovery-lifecycle.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/9999-y-mt76-recovery-lifecycle.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,4551 @@
+From: ACK72 <ACK72@users.noreply.github.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] mt76: complete channel operations and fail closed on recovery errors
+
+Always complete aborted scan/ROC software state, propagate channel errors,
+restore cached context on failure, and keep TX blocked by RESET on every
+PHY after MCU timeout. Balance the channel worker park before recovery
+takes it once under the mutex. Reject survey queries during recovery and
+make a racing wait interruptible, preserving normal ACS serialization.
+
+Adapt Gilly 047 NPU full-reset parity, additionally checking the stock NPU
+stop/idle acknowledgement before reclaiming DMA rings, checking every L1
+handshake and NPU restart, and retaining stopped queues after a failed
+restart. Use one full reset attempt rather than ten under the device mutex.
+Preserve offload, ring sizes and the packet data path. No new PCIe bus-reset
+protocol is claimed here.
+
+Refresh beacon monitoring only after successful L1 recovery; add bounded
+error-only channel/beacon diagnostics without changing the loss threshold.
+Gilly source: 0aa0666de1366b69d5d73d98c19809affc1f76ed, patch 047.
+
+Rebased onto mt76 2026-10-08, which reports aborted scans and ROC to
+mac80211 during a reset itself. A failed channel set now aborts the scan
+of its own radio, and ROC expiry keeps the upstream MT76_RESTART rule.
+
+Rebased onto mt76 2026-10-28, which aborts a running scan in change_chanctx
+itself and loads the beacon monitor interval once with acquire semantics.
+Only the failure warning remains in change_chanctx, and the beacon loss
+diagnostics use the loaded interval.
+
+A scan or ROC that cannot return to the operating channel, because the
+channel set fails or MCU recovery is running, leaves the phy off-channel:
+its TX stays gated and its beacons stopped, as the radio may still be on
+the other channel. A delayed work retries the return until it succeeds, a
+scan or ROC returns itself or the channel context is removed, and then
+ends the off-channel period for associated stations. mt7996_set_channel
+re-arms mac_work after any channel set outside MCU recovery, as upstream
+does.
+
+--- a/channel.c
++++ b/channel.c
+@@ -1,433 +1,515 @@
